#. text
#: launcher.cpp:258 launcher.cpp:3087
msgid "VSync"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:259
msgid "Wait for the display's refresh: no tearing."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:260
msgid "Frame rate cap"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:261
msgid "20 and 30: an even pace instead of the highest rate the PC reaches. 120, 144 and Unlocked (experimental): the game runs past its 60 at its own speed, as far as the PC and, with VSync, the monitor take it; frame generation is off with them, and the game goes back to 60 once it goes online for multiplayer. With frame generation, off follows the monitor."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:265
msgid "Frame rate display"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:266
msgid "On screen shows FPS, frame time, the CPU's, GPU's, PPU's, SPU's and RSX's load and a graph of the last frames' times, in the top right corner."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:268
msgid "Ultrawide"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:269
msgid "Draws the game to the full width of a wider screen. The HUD, menus and movies stay 16:9. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:270
msgid "Shader build indicator"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:271
msgid "A spinner in the bottom left corner while the game's new shaders are built, as RPCS3 shows."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:273
msgid "HDR10 on a display Windows has HDR on for (Settings, System, Display, Use HDR): the game's picture with its highlights raised toward the peak below, the rest at paper white. Not with frame generation. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:276
msgid "HDR peak brightness"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:277
msgid "How bright the brightest highlights get: fire, the sky, lightning. Auto takes what the display reports."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:278
msgid "HDR paper white"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:279
msgid "How bright white is in the rest of the picture and the HUD. Raise it in a bright room."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:280
msgid "Window style"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:281
msgid "How this window looks: Clean, smooth at every Windows scale, or Retro, a pixel font and 8-bit bevels. The game is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:283
msgid "Retro effects"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:284
msgid "Scanlines and a neon glow in this window, with the Retro window style. The game is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:285
msgid "Graphics card"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:286
msgid "Internal resolution"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:287
msgid "What the scene is drawn at. Shadow resolution and Effects resolution below say how large shadows, bloom and blur are drawn. AMD FSR and frame generation go no higher than the window."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:289
msgid "Shadow resolution"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:290
msgid "Shadow maps drawn larger: finer shadow edges and less stair-stepping, most of all at a high internal resolution; where the game's shadows are soft the change is small. 4x takes about 120 MB more video memory. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:293
msgid "Effects resolution"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:294
msgid "Bloom, blur and depth of field drawn at the internal resolution, not at the game's 640x360 and smaller: smoother blurred backgrounds and glow at 1440p and 4K, the game's brightness kept. Only with an internal resolution above 720p. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:297
msgid "Field of view"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:298
msgid "How wide the view is in play, against the game's: wider shows more around Kratos, narrower brings the view in. The in-engine cinematics keep the game's own. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:300
msgid "Ambient occlusion"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:301
msgid "Soft shade in corners, gaps and where things meet the ground, for a deeper picture, worked out from the scene's depth before the HUD goes on. High draws it at the internal resolution, On at half of it. Off with an ultrawide picture. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:304
msgid "Scaling"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:305
msgid "How the picture is scaled to the window. AMD FSR builds the detail from past frames, in place of SMAA, and FSR 1 takes over where there is no scene. NVIDIA DLSS does the same with NVIDIA's model on RTX cards (beta), its mode set by the internal resolution against the window (DLAA when they match); its DLL comes from NVIDIA's own GitHub when you pick it."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:309
msgid "FSR version"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:310
msgid "Auto takes the newest the card and its driver have: FSR 4.1 on AMD Radeon RX 6000 and newer (RX 6000: driver 26.10.1 or later), else FSR 3.1. 4.1 gives cleaner edges and thin lines; 3.1 keeps textures a little sharper and is lighter on the GPU."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:313
msgid "DLSS preset"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:314
msgid "Only with NVIDIA DLSS. Auto lets the DLL choose for each mode (K for DLAA, Quality and Balanced, M for Performance, L for Ultra Performance). L and M are sharper with less ghosting but cost more, best on RTX 40 and newer."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:316
msgid "FSR sharpening"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:317
msgid "The sharpening pass of FSR (RCAS). Only with FSR scaling."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:318
msgid "CAS sharpening"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:319
msgid "AMD's contrast adaptive sharpening on the picture with bilinear or sharp bilinear scaling, or NVIDIA DLSS: crisper detail, edges not overdone. AMD FSR has its own (FSR sharpening). Not with frame generation."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:321
msgid "Debanding"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:322
msgid "Smooths the steps in dark gradients, fog and skies, with a fine grain; edges and texture stay as they are. Not with frame generation."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:324
msgid "Colour vibrance"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:325
msgid "Livelier colours: the dull ones raised the most, skin and colours that are strong already far less. On the whole picture, the game's HUD and menus too."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:327
msgid "Contrast"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:328
msgid "Lit surfaces and highlights stand out more; deep shadows keep their detail, black and white kept."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:329 launcher.cpp:4742
msgid "Frame generation"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:330
msgid "Twice the frames on screen, with VSync on: the game is held at half the monitor's refresh rate (60 at 120 Hz), a frame is made between each two, about a frame later, and below 25 it stands aside. ANR FG (beta) keeps what moves whole where AMD FSR's can tear it; chosen, the launcher offers to download it from Apex Compute's releases."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:333
msgid "NVIDIA Reflex"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:334
msgid "Less input lag on NVIDIA GeForce GTX 900 and newer (beta): each frame starts as late as the GPU allows, so fewer frames wait their turn when the GPU is the slower part. Boost keeps the GPU's clocks up too. Not with frame generation. Takes effect at the next start."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:337
msgid "Anti-aliasing"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:338
msgid "Smooths jagged edges after the game has drawn the frame. Costs next to nothing. AMD FSR scaling does this itself in play."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:340
msgid "Anisotropic filtering"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:341
msgid "Sharper textures seen at an angle. The game itself asks for none."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:342
msgid "Build shaders in the background"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:343
msgid "A new shader is built while the game goes on, instead of a stall. Walls, floors and other solid things wait for theirs; an effect turns up a moment late."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:345
msgid "Wait for new shaders"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:346
msgid "How long walls and floors wait for their new shaders. Short: 33 ms in all for a frame, no pause; past it a gap shows there until the shader is built. Full: up to two seconds each, no gap but a pause. Off: no wait, a gap for a moment."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:349
msgid "Render thread"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:350
msgid "The GPU's work is recorded and shown on a thread of its own, beside the one that reads the game's commands: about 10% more frames where that one holds the game back."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:352
msgid "Build pipelines first"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:353
msgid "At the start the game waits until the pipelines kept from earlier sessions are built, so none is built while you play: a moment, a few seconds after a GPU driver update."
msgstr ""

#. check_line
#: launcher.cpp:355 launcher.cpp:2978
msgid "Pixel shaders built ahead"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:356
msgid "The pixel shaders of the game's files are built before play, after the vertex shaders on the first start (Enter or Start leaves them for the next), or by Build all shaders now below Clear shaders: some minutes, once. Places you reach later wait for fewer of them."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:359
msgid "Device"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:360
msgid "Auto reads a controller and the keyboard and mouse at the same time: either one plays."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:361
msgid "Controller API"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:362
msgid "Auto reads a controller through XInput when it has it (Xbox, most PC pads), else through SDL3 (DualShock 4, DualSense, Switch and others). With DS4Windows, XInput, or one controller counts twice."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:364
msgid "Stick dead zone"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:365
msgid "How far a stick moves before it counts."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:366
msgid "Confirm button"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:367
msgid "The button that confirms in the menus."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:368
msgid "Vibration"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:368
msgid "Controller rumble."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:369
msgid "Damage to Kratos"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:370
msgid "How much of a hit he takes. None: hits take no health from him."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:371
msgid "Kratos's damage"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:372
msgid "How much his hits take from an enemy. One hit: all of its health."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:373
msgid "Max red orbs"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:374
msgid "The red orbs are held at the most the game allows, 1,000,000. A save made with this on keeps them."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:375
msgid "Infinite magic and items"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:376
msgid "The magic and item meters stay full."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:377
msgid "Infinite rage"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:378
msgid "The rage meter stays full."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:379
msgid "Infinite double jumps"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:380
msgid "Kratos can jump again in the air, as often as he likes."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:381
msgid "Use mods"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:382
msgid "Off: the game as it is, every mod left out. Below, each one is switched on its own."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:383
msgid "Write out the game's textures"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:384
msgid "For making texture mods: each texture the game loads goes once into textures-dump beside the settings, named by the id a picture in its place takes. The game is slower while it is on."
msgstr ""

#. text
#: launcher.cpp:386 launcher.cpp:2623 launcher.cpp:3105
msgid "Multiplayer"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:387
msgid "Auto: the game finds other players itself, as torrents find their peers: no host. Host: this PC runs the matchmaking, for its own game and the players who join it. Join: play through a host's PC. Then Multi-Player on the game's title screen, and Quick Play."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:390
msgid "Online ID"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:391
msgid "Your name in the game: 3 to 16 letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter. Every player needs their own."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:393
msgid "Host's address"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:394
msgid "To join: the address the host's Multiplayer tab shows, or the host's name."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:395
msgid "Always relayed"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:396
msgid "Your game's traffic goes by the host's PC (Host, Join) or the players' nodes (Auto) instead of straight to the other players: for a network where joining works and playing does not."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:398
msgid "Open the port on the router"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:399
msgid "Auto: asks the router (UPnP) to let other players reach this PC, as torrent clients do. Players who can be reached carry for the ones who cannot."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:401
msgid "Help others connect"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:402
msgid "Auto: two players who cannot reach each other may talk through your PC (a few pairs at most)."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:403
msgid "Community nodes"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:404
msgid "Auto: nodes anyone can run on a reachable PC (scripts\\mp_p2p.py community), which introduce players and carry for them: address:port, a comma between."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:406
msgid "Launcher language"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:407
msgid "The language of this window. Windows language follows Windows' display language, and English where this window has no translation. The game's own text and speech are the next row's."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:409
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:410
msgid "The game's language: text and speech. The EU disc takes it at its first start, where it asks (Cross for this one, Triangle for Greek), and keeps it."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:412
msgid "Esc closes the game"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:413
msgid "Esc is not a PS3 button; off leaves it free."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:414
msgid "Save backups"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:415
msgid "Copies kept of a save before the game writes over it."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:416
msgid "Steady audio"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:417
msgid "Runs the game's sound on a thread of its own, so heavy fights do not break it up."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:418
msgid "Speakers"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:419
msgid "Auto follows the output device; 7.1 for Windows Sonic or Dolby Atmos for Headphones. Surround also needs the game's Sound Mode (Options, Audio) on 5.1 or 7.1."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:421
msgid "Bypass sound effects"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:422
msgid "The game's sound skips Windows' and the sound card's effects (equalizers, loudness, virtual surround), where the device has a way past them."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:424
msgid "Precompile music"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:425
msgid "Music on the screen that builds the shaders at a version's first start, made by the program."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:426
msgid "Optimise for this PC"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:427
msgid "When the game's code is built, a training copy first plays the opening by itself, muted, in a window of its own (leave it open), and the build then uses what it counted: 2-3% more frames on the test laptop. It adds about 15 minutes to each build; if anything goes wrong there, the build goes on without it. Turned on after a build, Play builds the game's code again with it."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:431
msgid "Show this window at start"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:432
msgid "When off, hold Shift while the game starts to bring it back."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:433
msgid "Check for updates"
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:434
msgid "At most every six hours, asks GitHub whether a newer release is out, and says so here with a link to it."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:452
msgid "The PS3's SPU anti-aliasing, whose picture this port never shows, does no work: about 5% faster, and the bloom stays. AMD FSR and frame generation take the game's order without MLAA, which has no bloom or motion blur."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:455
msgid "The blur of what lies outside the camera's focus."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:456
msgid "No blur of what moves fast. With AMD FSR or frame generation it never reaches the screen anyway, and they keep its draws, for what moves."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:458
msgid "Keeps the triangles the game drops as too thin for its 720p grid. For Internal resolution above 720p: at 720p it only adds geometry (3% slower at the first level, 11% at the gate)."
msgstr ""

#: launcher.cpp:461
msgid "No dynamic shadows: the biggest saving, about 25% faster in the Megaera fight."
msgstr ""

